# Cesium ion access token.
#
# The simulator streams real satellite imagery and global terrain from Cesium
# ion, and cannot draw a world without a token. There is no need to set one
# here to fly: the application asks for one on its first run and keeps it in
# the browser, and it is changed afterwards under Settings -> Cesium ion.
#
# This is the other way in, for a build run from a checkout: a token here is
# compiled into the bundle and is what the application starts with. It is a
# default rather than the last word — a token entered in the application
# overrides it for that browser.
#
# Get a free token at https://ion.cesium.com/tokens
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste your token below.
#
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_` values are inlined at build time, so a running dev server has
# to be restarted to pick up a change here.
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored. Never commit a real token.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=

# Google Maps Platform API key — optional, and not needed to start.
#
# The "Photorealistic" world detail setting streams Google's photogrammetry
# mesh: buildings, trees and forests as real geometry rather than as pixels
# painted onto the terrain. By default those tiles come through Cesium ion on
# the token above, which is included in ion's free non-commercial plan.
#
# A key here bypasses ion and bills Google directly instead, which is what a
# project past ion's monthly allowance wants. Create one at
# https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis/credentials with the
# "Map Tiles API" enabled, and restrict it to your own domains.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
